# Firmware images and community archives are stored as plain git blobs.
#
# Rationale: the Git LFS endpoint (lfs.github.com) was unreachable / unusably
# slow from the environment this repository was assembled in (all LFS object
# uploads ended in EOF / stalled), while the regular git HTTPS endpoint
# works reliably. Every file in firmware/ is below GitHub's 100 MB per-file
# limit, so plain blobs are sufficient and keep the archive self-contained.
#
# Files are stored as LZMA (.BIN.lzma) to keep the repo size manageable;
# `firmware/MANIFEST.sha256` records the SHA-256 of every stored file AND of
# the original .BIN recovered from it, so integrity can be verified with
# `python tools/verify_firmware_bundle.py --deep`.

# Build/temp artefacts
*.pyc
__pycache__/
